 "toleranceNote": "Upstream's own calls against the port's list. The PNG goes through ports of Chrome's own sampling (Skia's bitmap sampler with its 4-bit bilinear weights, the spans it maps from) and coverage, and the placeholders through the port's scan conversion of upstream's SVG paths, so against Chrome 153 every pixel is within 2 levels but for 8 on the rotated, mirrored placeholder: where its icon touches the edge of the drawImage destination under a rotation, Chrome's clip to the destination leaves pixels whose centres are outside it empty and thins those just inside (up to 17 levels), which neither an anti-aliased nor a whole-pixel clip reproduces. 16 pixels leaves room for another Chrome build.",
